  "notes": "From English \"memo\" + する. One of the most common loanword + する combinations in everyday Japanese. Used casually for quick, informal note-taking — writing on sticky notes, typing into a phone, scribbling on paper. More casual than {記録|きろく}する or {書|か}き{留|と}める.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- メモを{取|と}る: to take notes (noun + {取|と}る form is equally common)\n- メモ{帳|ちょう}: memo pad; notepad\n- メモ{用紙|ようし}: memo paper\n- {付箋|ふせん}にメモする: to write a memo on a sticky note\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {記録|きろく}する: to record — more formal and thorough; implies an official or complete record\n- {書|か}き{留|と}める: to write down; to note — slightly more formal than メモする\n- ノートを{取|と}る: to take notes — specifically in a notebook, often in lectures or classes",
